{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And on the first day.</b> It is the day of the exodus from Egypt, and the seventh day is the day of Pharaoh's drowning, as I shall explain." "<b>All melakhah.</b> In all the festivals, apart from the Sabbath and the Day of Atonement, \"all melakhah\" is not written concerning them; only concerning Passover alone does it say it, and it conditioned it to exclude food for the soul. And everywhere — whether in Passover, in Atzeret, in the Day of Remembrance, or in the festival of Sukkot — it holds to a brief way of saying \"all melakhah you shall not do.\" Only in one place, in Passover, \"you shall not do all melakhah,\" in the manner that it mentioned at the outset."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {1 "Resolved 'the Day of Remembrance' (יום הזכרון) as the standard designation for Rosh HaShanah; left Atzeret untranslated as Ibn Ezra's term for Shavuot."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:33:38.234315405Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}